    {
      "label": "Do you have to…?",
      "intro": {
        "text": "Have to ведёт себя как обычный глагол: в вопросе и отрицании нужны do, does, did. Don't have to значит «не обязательно», а не «нельзя»: You don't have to come — можешь не приходить.",
        "highlights": [
          {
            "text": "do, does, did",
            "color": "info",
            "style": "bold"
          },
          {
            "text": "Don't have to",
            "color": "term",
            "style": "bold"
          },
          {
            "text": "не обязательно",
            "color": "example",
            "style": "bold_underline"
          }
        ]
      },
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Отрицание",
          "borderColor": "bad",
          "rules": [
            {
              "name": "don't have to",
              "suffix": "не обязательно",
              "example": "You don't have to come."
            },
            {
              "name": "doesn't have to",
              "suffix": "для he / she / it",
              "example": "He doesn't have to work today."
            },
            {
              "name": "didn't have to",
              "suffix": "в прошлом",
              "example": "I didn't have to pay."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Вопрос",
          "borderColor": "info",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "Do you have to work on Sunday?",
